The files under src/main/resources/org/jebol/mezz/ are unmodified copies
of Rebol's own library, taken from src/mezz/ upstream. They are loaded
and evaluated at startup, and they are the part of the borrowed code that
ships: they are inside the jar under org/jebol/mezz/, and thus inside the
distribution archive. They are the larger part of that jar.

The files under src/test/resources/rebol-suite/ are unmodified test
scripts, taken from src/tests/ upstream. They do not ship.

They are vendored rather than fetched so the suite is reproducible
without a network, and they are kept byte-for-byte as published so that
a failure is unambiguously ours. Where JEBOL cannot yet satisfy one, the
gap is recorded in src/test/resources/rebol-suite/known-gaps.txt rather
than by editing the script.

